## 2026-08-18 09:35 — MariaDB is now the live source of truth (cutover); retention export made streaming-safe; a false "stall" that was my monitoring bug

WHAT. Cut the live bot fully over to the MariaDB backend (config.toml type=mariadb,
run bare — no more `--db guild_log.db` shim). MariaDB now holds the go-forward
truth; the 6.3 GB sqlite guild_log.db is retained as a cold backup and stays in
the code as a selectable backend. Run #27 (mariadb, explorer/0.9.0) is live,
screen-hosted (durable), growing; sqlite is frozen.

ENABLING FIX (committed 66e2732). export_run read a whole run's frames through the
seam's default cursor, which is BUFFERED on MariaDB — it would materialise a
multi-GB run in memory. Since retention prunes only after a verified archive, a
broken archiver = the disk fills (~7 GiB/day). Added Connection.execute_stream
(unbuffered on MariaDB, native stream on SQLite) and used it in export_run.
Verified: a real 9,480-frame run exports at 3 MB peak RSS (flat = streaming). Unit
guard + live roundtrip export test, both green.

CORRECTION — the "MariaDB stalls under live play" claim was WRONG; it was a
measurement artifact, not a bug. I watched run #24/#25 with a REUSED db.connect()
connection (autocommit=False) across sleeps; InnoDB's default REPEATABLE READ
pinned that connection to its first snapshot, so COUNT(*) never advanced even
though the bot was committing normally. I mistook the frozen snapshot for a hung
bot, killed two healthy MariaDB runs, and briefly reverted to sqlite. Fresh-
connection queries proved the truth: run #24 reached 3,024 frames (tick 411962),
run #25 reached 1,865 — both playing fine. Per-frame MariaDB write cost is ~25 ms
(frame 4.4 ms + ~150-400 tiles at ~15 ms + a few plain-INSERT executemany),
comfortably under the ~62 ms frame budget. So: NO async queue / Valkey / writer-
thread is needed — synchronous writes keep up. LESSON: when checking live write
progress on MariaDB, use a FRESH connection (or autocommit / READ COMMITTED) per
sample, never a reused REPEATABLE-READ connection.

VERIFY. Full suite 151 passed / 1 skipped; reaper gate GREEN (151 in the pinned
container, clean imports of db.py/archive.py); STEEMER_TEST_MARIADB=1 roundtrip
(incl. the new export streaming) green. Post-cutover, run #27 monitored with fresh
connections: frames 143->273->404->516... climbing steadily, ticks advancing, no
stall; sqlite guild_log.db frozen. Bot tree roots at the screen daemon (PID 1672).

OPS NOTES. config.toml=mariadb is now the live truth — a bare `make run-live`
does the right thing; no shim. Retention cron (04:17) archives+prunes from
MariaDB, now safe via the streaming export. reclaim after prune is a MariaDB
no-op (InnoDB reuses freed pages; OPTIMIZE TABLE only if the file must shrink).
Dangling-open MariaDB run rows from the killed #24/#25 episode are closed by
begin_run's defensive close on the next start.

## 2026-08-18 10:43 — explorer/0.10.0: kill the embark/recruit duplicate-send storm (phantom-character family) + start M3a smelt; and fix read-only MariaDB snapshot pinning

**What.** Three changes this iteration:

1. **In-flight guard on guild commands (the phantom-character fix).** `village()`
   re-issued the *same* `embark`/`recruit` every tick because it decides on a
   few-tick-stale village frame — the just-commanded char still shows in
   `chars_here` before the command lands. So run #28 sent **3135 embarks for ~28
   chars**, and the tail bounced `no_such_character` (294) / `roster_cap` (48)
   once the char finally left. Fix: track the tick each char was embarked
   (`self._embark_at`) and each recruit (`self._recruit_at`); skip re-sending
   while one is in flight (`EMBARK_COOLDOWN`/`RECRUIT_COOLDOWN` = 8 ticks), prune
   the record once the char leaves `chars_here`, and count in-flight embarks
   toward `world_cap` so we don't over-deploy distinct chars either.

2. **M3a smelt (ore → ingot).** The guild loots `ore_copper`/`ore_iron`
   (`uses=['smelt']`) and was *selling* it. Now, in the village, a char holding a
   matching ore pair `smelt`s them into an ingot (metal feedstock); paired ore is
   kept, stranded singles still sold (the v0.8.0 anti-clog rule). `smelt` needs no
   per-world vocabulary. **`forge` is deliberately NOT wired** — it requires a
   per-world `product` NAME that no `forged` event in all history reveals, and a
   guessed product is an `unknown_product` action error (unlike a blind brew,
   where the pot infers the product and never errors). Forging lands once a
   product name is learned.

3. **Read-only MariaDB snapshot fix (operator-reported "analysis gated on
   read-only reads").** `db.connect(readonly=True)` opened MariaDB
   `autocommit=False` under InnoDB's default REPEATABLE READ, so a reader held
   across samples froze an MVCC snapshot at its first SELECT and never saw the
   running bot's new rows (and left an open txn pinning a metadata lock + undo
   history). This was the code-level cause the earlier "monitoring artifact" note
   only worked around by habit. Fix: readonly connections now open
   `autocommit=True` under READ COMMITTED — each SELECT is a fresh
   statement-consistent read.

**Why.** The phantom-character family was the single largest live-backend error
class (~60% of MariaDB-window errors). The diagnosis in the analyze phase (and
the operator's "new players" steer) both pointed at it, but the DB drill-down
showed it is NOT rival players (all failing uids are our own guild `g_cd0e2a_*`)
— it is a self-inflicted duplicate-send storm. M3a is the top durability lever
(armor is unbuyable; forging is the only armor route) and smelt is its safe,
non-speculative first step. The read-only fix unblocks the operator's analysis
tooling.

**Expected effect.**
- Phantom-character *embark/recruit* errors (`no_such_character` + `roster_cap` +
  village-side `not_in_village`) should fall sharply next window — a run-#28
  village-frame replay through 0.10.0 produced **0 same-char re-embarks within 8
  ticks vs 3151 in a 0.9.0 sim**, and recruit sends dropped 87→11.
- The *field* `move`/`attack` `unknown_character` remainder should be roughly
  UNCHANGED (it is a server-lag death-echo of moves queued for a char that died
  mid-field — not addressed here, and not bot-fixable from the frame).
- Smelt: ingots begin appearing + `smelt`/craft-complete events accrue (the M3a
  learning foundation); net carry neutral-to-lower (2 ore → 1 ingot).
- No gold-signal change expected (gold_delta ≈ 0; the lever remains throughput +
  survival).

