## 2026-08-18 12:37 — explorer/0.11.0: authoritative roster gating via the public /api/spectate/guilds endpoint

**What.** The recruit/embark gates now use the TRUE roster from the server's
public web endpoint instead of the lagged/partial village-frame snapshot.
`steemer/spectate.py` `SpectateRoster` polls `GET /api/spectate/guilds` on a
background daemon thread (every 45s, 5s timeout, best-effort), parses our guild's
`characters` (total) and per-char `world` into `(total, {field_world: n}, home)`,
and caches it (marked unavailable if a fetch hasn't succeeded within 3× the poll
interval). The live runner attaches it as `bot.spectate`, warms it with one fetch
before the first frame, and stops it on exit. `explorer.village()` gates recruit
on the authoritative `total` vs `roster_cap` and embark on the authoritative
`fielded`/per-world vs `world_cap`/`party_cap`, **falling back to the frame
snapshot** when spectate is stale/absent. The embark TARGET char still comes from
the frame's `chars_here` (only a char the frame shows home can embark). Tests and
offline replay have no `bot.spectate`, so they use the snapshot fallback and
never touch the network (`--no-spectate` also disables it).

**Why.** The frame `guild` snapshot is a partial view of a large persistent
roster (the server shows chars intermittently — gaps ~350 ticks; count swings
30->6->30 with ~no deaths), so gating on it over-recruits (`roster_cap`) and
over-embarks. The count can't be reconstructed from frames, but the web endpoint
returns it directly. Discovered by vendoring the web client (git ccb4123).

**HTTP base** derives from the token's ZeroMQ `server` (`tcp://host:port` ->
`https://host`), so no new config; default `https://bot.willmorrison.net`.

**Expected effect.** `roster_cap` rejections should fall further (0.10.0's
cooldown already cut them 87->11; authoritative gating should approach 0 — we
stop recruiting the moment the TRUE roster hits the cap, not when the swinging
snapshot briefly reads low). Embark/`world_cap` waste similarly. Gameplay
throughput otherwise unchanged. **Falsified if** `roster_cap` (and `world_cap`)
error rates do NOT fall vs the run #32/#33 baseline, or if the bot under-deploys
(idle home chars while fielded < world_cap) — which would mean the authoritative
`fielded` is over-counting (e.g. dead chars lingering in the spectate roster).

**Verify.** pytest 177 passed / 2 skipped; new tests/test_spectate.py +
authoritative-gating tests in test_decision_engine.py, mutation-checked (gate
ignoring spectate, and the home=total-fielded split, both caught). Live fetch of
/api/spectate/guilds verified (our guild total=22, fielded vale:5/mines:1/spire:1,
home 15). Replay clean on 0.11.0 (snapshot fallback). Reaper gate: pending.
Redeploy needed (bot restart) for it to go live.

